1
00:00:06,873 --> 00:00:08,708
MICHIKO DAIMON
FREELANCE SURGEON

2
00:00:08,775 --> 00:00:10,143
<i>The test results</i>

3
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:11,344
<i>are positive.</i>

4
00:00:11,411 --> 00:00:13,146
- Demon!
- Dr. Daimon!

5
00:00:13,213 --> 00:00:15,015
- Dr. Daimon!
- Michiko!

6
00:00:15,548 --> 00:00:19,686
I've… been infected…

7
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:31,131
Faster! Harder!

8
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:33,733
Harder! Michiko!

9
00:00:45,779 --> 00:00:49,282
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

10
00:00:50,984 --> 00:00:54,187
Let's see…

11
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:57,857
We got a postcard from Dr. Ichiki.

12
00:00:57,924 --> 00:00:58,758
Really?

13
00:00:58,825 --> 00:01:00,360
It's from Nigeria!

14
00:01:00,427 --> 00:01:01,261
Really?

15
00:01:01,327 --> 00:01:03,997
"If it hadn't been for you, Dr. Daimon,

16
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:07,167
I would have died three months ago."

17
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:10,236
"I've given up being a little lost lamb

18
00:01:10,303 --> 00:01:12,939
and I will do my best in Africa again."

19
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:17,310
"With heartfelt appreciation, Kei Ichiki."

20
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,647
- So he went back.
- Yes.

21
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:22,248
He's with elephants. How cute.

22
00:01:22,315 --> 00:01:23,249
Yes.

23
00:01:23,983 --> 00:01:25,351
What are you doing?

24
00:01:26,319 --> 00:01:28,388
- Come on!
- It could be <i>papin.</i>

25
00:01:28,455 --> 00:01:31,791
- You're practicing touch reading?
- I think it's <i>chupin!</i>

26
00:01:38,498 --> 00:01:40,967
Practicing suturing with 4-0 thread?

27
00:01:41,734 --> 00:01:43,336
On score sticks?

28
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:52,112
- Don't move.
- Okay.

29
00:01:53,546 --> 00:01:56,516
Thank you. That had just come undone.

30
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:58,351
- Who said you could look?
- What?

31
00:01:59,252 --> 00:02:00,954
- So that's what you're up to!
- Whoa!

32
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:03,690
You've completely recovered now!

33
00:02:03,756 --> 00:02:06,926
And COVID is finally under control too.

34
00:02:06,993 --> 00:02:08,795
Michiko Daimon is back!

35
00:02:08,862 --> 00:02:09,729
Yes!

36
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:13,066
I want to hurry up and do surgeries!

37
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,335
- Don't be hasty, Michiko.
- What?

38
00:02:15,401 --> 00:02:16,236
<i>Ron!</i>

39
00:02:18,171 --> 00:02:20,373
<i>Honitsu</i> with three <i>dora.</i>

40
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,774
<i>Baiman!</i>

41
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,679
And I just sewed that up too!

42
00:02:26,746 --> 00:02:28,314
Michiko!

43
00:02:28,381 --> 00:02:29,983
BEN CASEY, GANNON

44
00:02:30,683 --> 00:02:32,685
<i>2021.</i>

45
00:02:32,752 --> 00:02:35,855
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

46
00:02:36,422 --> 00:02:38,892
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

47
00:02:39,526 --> 00:02:41,427
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

48
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,630
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

49
00:02:43,696 --> 00:02:46,900
<i>have firmly withstood the storm.</i>

50
00:03:08,288 --> 00:03:11,157
RYUTARO HACHISUKA
DIRECTOR OF INTERNAL MEDICINE

51
00:03:15,094 --> 00:03:16,896
Good morning, Director Hachisuka.

52
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:21,434
Good morning.

53
00:03:21,501 --> 00:03:23,536
There is a super doctor here to see you.

54
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:25,071
Come in.

55
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:35,481
Dr. Hachisuka.

56
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:42,589
I've been expecting you, Dr. Korogi.

57
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:45,625
We need your skills.

58
00:03:52,599 --> 00:03:55,268
<i>However,</i>
<i>the university hospital's once illustrious</i>

59
00:03:55,335 --> 00:03:58,271
<i>Surgery Department was moved</i>
<i>to the branch hospital.</i>

60
00:03:58,338 --> 00:04:00,573
<i>The number of surgeries</i>
<i>was greatly decreased</i>

61
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:03,409
<i>and it was running in the red.</i>

62
00:04:03,476 --> 00:04:07,480
I swear that our Surgery Department will…

63
00:04:08,781 --> 00:04:10,550
return to the main hospital.

64
00:04:10,617 --> 00:04:14,721
And we'll kick out
that arrogant Director Hachisuka.

65
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:18,691
- It is the one thought that…
- Yes, sir.

66
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:24,230
I'm talking.

67
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:25,398
I know.

68
00:04:25,465 --> 00:04:27,000
Then why the "yes, sir"?

69
00:04:27,567 --> 00:04:28,735
Sorry.

70
00:04:28,801 --> 00:04:30,136
You're spreading droplets.

71
00:04:30,203 --> 00:04:31,271
Sorry.

72
00:04:31,337 --> 00:04:33,139
You really have no sense of timing.

73
00:04:33,206 --> 00:04:34,741
- Sorry.
- What's with you?

74
00:04:35,508 --> 00:04:38,645
Do you think I'm being abusive right now?

75
00:04:38,711 --> 00:04:42,015
No. Absolutely not. Not even a little bit.

76
00:04:42,081 --> 00:04:43,449
That's right.

77
00:04:43,516 --> 00:04:46,085
Branch Director Hiruma
is in a bad mood today.

78
00:04:46,152 --> 00:04:47,720
- He sure is.
- What's that?

79
00:04:48,421 --> 00:04:49,355
Did you say something?

80
00:04:49,922 --> 00:04:51,057
- No!
- No!

81
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,626
I am not in a bad mood, you know.

82
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:57,063
I'm actually being very kind.

83
00:04:57,664 --> 00:04:59,232
Right, Dr. Kaji?

84
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:00,366
What?

85
00:05:00,433 --> 00:05:03,569
Am I being abusive right now?

86
00:05:03,636 --> 00:05:05,004
No.

87
00:05:05,571 --> 00:05:08,274
Not even a little bit.

88
00:05:08,341 --> 00:05:09,642
That's right.

89
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:10,777
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

90
00:05:11,544 --> 00:05:12,679
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

91
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,314
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

92
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:16,749
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

93
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:21,421
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

94
00:05:21,954 --> 00:05:22,955
Dr. Daimon!

95
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,024
You don't have Lassa fever anymore?

96
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:29,996
Oh, my. What a magnificent outfit,
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

97
00:05:30,063 --> 00:05:32,799
Such beautiful legs. Thank you!

98
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,735
<i>This woman…</i>

99
00:05:36,536 --> 00:05:37,603
That's sexual harassment.

100
00:05:38,638 --> 00:05:39,806
I'm sorry.

101
00:05:39,872 --> 00:05:41,140
<i>She hates groups,</i>

102
00:05:41,207 --> 00:05:42,508
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

103
00:05:42,575 --> 00:05:44,377
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

104
00:05:44,877 --> 00:05:48,147
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

105
00:05:48,214 --> 00:05:50,083
<i>to work her way up.</i>

106
00:05:51,317 --> 00:05:53,219
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

107
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:57,123
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

108
00:06:21,681 --> 00:06:25,952
I see a lot more people
in the entertainment districts now.

109
00:06:26,519 --> 00:06:28,521
<i>Yes, it is very troubling.</i>

110
00:06:28,588 --> 00:06:31,724
What? Director Hachisuka
used to be on the surgical staff?

111
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:33,926
Yes. But that was a long time ago.

112
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:37,597
He enrolled two years after Director Ebina
and one year after me.

113
00:06:38,664 --> 00:06:40,133
- Is that right?
- Yes.

114
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:41,067
TAKASHI EBINA
DIRECTOR OF SURGERY

115
00:06:41,868 --> 00:06:44,504
Hachisuka was all brains and theory.

116
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,439
He was totally useless as a surgeon.

117
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:50,243
He didn't have the one thing
you need to be a medical staff.

118
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:53,312
What is the one thing you need?

119
00:06:53,379 --> 00:06:56,282
Concern and attentiveness
for the professors, obviously.

120
00:06:56,349 --> 00:06:59,652
But most of all, reading their minds
and doing what they expect.

121
00:07:02,121 --> 00:07:03,022
Yes, sir.

122
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:04,657
Hey.

123
00:07:04,724 --> 00:07:06,559
Your eyes are watering. Are you okay?

124
00:07:09,529 --> 00:07:12,965
Dr. Hiruma was Director of Surgery
at that time and found him annoying,

125
00:07:13,032 --> 00:07:15,268
so he was booted off the medical staff

126
00:07:15,334 --> 00:07:18,438
and he was transferred
to the boring infectious disease lab.

127
00:07:18,504 --> 00:07:20,239
But look at him now.

128
00:07:20,306 --> 00:07:23,209
He has surpassed his seniors
thanks to COVID, huh?

129
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:24,377
<i>Have you forgotten?</i>

130
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,646
<i>If there is another surge</i>

131
00:07:27,313 --> 00:07:30,416
<i>in infections like the past</i>
<i>due to letting down our guard,</i>

132
00:07:31,317 --> 00:07:33,686
<i>I, Hachisuka, will once again…</i>

133
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:36,756
<i>order a state of emergency!</i>

134
00:07:36,823 --> 00:07:39,192
- Hey! Wait a minute here!
- Is he serious?

135
00:07:39,258 --> 00:07:41,194
Who do you think you are? Prime Minister?

136
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:43,429
You don't have that right, you jerk!

137
00:07:43,496 --> 00:07:44,530
- That's right!
- Yes!

138
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,800
Hey, Dr. Daimon,

139
00:07:47,867 --> 00:07:50,903
since we got pushed into
this tiny branch hospital

140
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,371
and we are always working remotely,

141
00:07:52,438 --> 00:07:54,207
there are no assigned desks.

142
00:07:54,707 --> 00:07:57,810
So you can sit where you like.
But not there. That's mine.

143
00:08:03,382 --> 00:08:04,550
Cut that out!

144
00:08:04,617 --> 00:08:06,252
Are you some kind of monster?

145
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,288
You are such a clueless woman.

146
00:08:09,355 --> 00:08:11,023
There's no assigned seating, right?

147
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,326
Hey!

148
00:08:13,392 --> 00:08:16,963
But Director Ebina
isn't used to not having a desk.

149
00:08:17,029 --> 00:08:20,700
It took him three months
to finally build this fort of serenity.

150
00:08:20,766 --> 00:08:22,602
- Is that right?
- You can't tell?

151
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:25,571
Who cares about that!
Hurry up and give me some surgeries!

152
00:08:25,638 --> 00:08:26,906
- Hey!
- Hey!

153
00:08:26,973 --> 00:08:30,076
Even us guys rarely get to do surgery!

154
00:08:30,142 --> 00:08:31,677
We hardly have any surgeries

155
00:08:31,744 --> 00:08:32,879
due to COVID and that guy!

156
00:08:32,945 --> 00:08:34,313
- Complain to him!
- Yes!

157
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:38,317
<i>You think we must impose a state</i>
<i>of emergency and be more careful?</i>

158
00:08:39,151 --> 00:08:40,253
<i>Yes, I do.</i>

159
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:43,289
COVID has put us all on edge.

160
00:08:44,123 --> 00:08:45,124
Dr. Daimon,

161
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:48,794
I'll sit over here at this table,
all right?

162
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:50,530
So don't sit here. Okay?

163
00:08:52,298 --> 00:08:53,533
Your face.

164
00:08:55,401 --> 00:08:56,335
It's frightening?

165
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:01,707
<i>Thank you for your opinion, Dr. Hachisuka.</i>

166
00:09:01,774 --> 00:09:03,576
<i>It's been nice talking…</i>

167
00:09:04,176 --> 00:09:05,645
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

168
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:06,846
Jeez.

169
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,550
I'm alternating
between anger and irritation.

170
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:12,485
You know what this is?

171
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:13,619
It's stress.

172
00:09:17,256 --> 00:09:18,591
I'll do an inspection.

173
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,428
Secretly…

174
00:09:23,596 --> 00:09:24,664
in Ginza.

175
00:09:25,765 --> 00:09:27,366
Time for an inspection.

176
00:09:31,938 --> 00:09:33,539
Dr. Ebina! Disinfect your hands!

177
00:09:33,606 --> 00:09:34,507
Oh, sorry.

178
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:36,475
I was so excited, I forgot.

179
00:09:36,542 --> 00:09:38,044
- Hurry!
- Coming!

180
00:09:38,611 --> 00:09:40,012
Oh, Branch Director Hiruma!

181
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:41,714
You got here early! Sorry!

182
00:09:41,781 --> 00:09:45,718
Thank you so much for inviting us
to such a high-class place!

183
00:09:45,785 --> 00:09:48,254
Quit calling me "Branch Director."

184
00:09:48,321 --> 00:09:51,557
Why do you think
I'm wearing these clothes?

185
00:09:51,624 --> 00:09:53,225
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

186
00:09:53,292 --> 00:09:56,796
Today, I am not a doctor.

187
00:09:56,862 --> 00:10:00,099
Think of me as a mob boss.

188
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,968
Boss, huh?

189
00:10:02,034 --> 00:10:04,337
Then how about we call you "uncle"?

190
00:10:04,403 --> 00:10:05,871
I like it. Call me that.

191
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:07,139
- Uncle Hiruma.
- Uncle Hiruma.

192
00:10:07,206 --> 00:10:08,674
Oh, yes!

193
00:10:08,741 --> 00:10:10,142
Dr. Ebina,

194
00:10:10,209 --> 00:10:11,711
it has been such a long time.

195
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:14,080
Hello, Mayako Mama. It has been a while.

196
00:10:15,081 --> 00:10:16,482
- Here.
- Thank you.

197
00:10:17,249 --> 00:10:18,684
I'm Dr. Kaji. Nice to meet you.

198
00:10:18,751 --> 00:10:20,586
- I am Mayako.
- Thank you.

199
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,622
As you can see,

200
00:10:22,688 --> 00:10:24,557
business is very slow.

201
00:10:25,224 --> 00:10:26,993
Thank you for coming.

202
00:10:27,059 --> 00:10:30,096
Shigeka-chan, you've always been so kind.

203
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:32,398
Maya-chan, I love you.

204
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:35,267
"Shigeka-chan?"

205
00:10:36,402 --> 00:10:37,403
So…

206
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,705
where are the other hostesses?

207
00:10:41,007 --> 00:10:41,841
Dr. Kaji,

208
00:10:41,907 --> 00:10:43,242
you know what times are like.

209
00:10:43,776 --> 00:10:44,610
Right now,

210
00:10:44,677 --> 00:10:47,647
none of the hostesses are coming to work.

211
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,215
Today,

212
00:10:49,281 --> 00:10:53,386
think of Dr. Ebina as your hostess
and enjoy.

213
00:10:56,589 --> 00:10:59,125
You really are a friend in need.

214
00:10:59,191 --> 00:11:01,594
I came here alone from Hiroshima

215
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:04,096
and opened this place in glorious Ginza.

216
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,165
But COVID wiped out my income.

217
00:11:06,232 --> 00:11:08,267
I was about to close up shop.

218
00:11:09,402 --> 00:11:10,369
Don't!

219
00:11:11,303 --> 00:11:13,005
Don't run away, Mama.

220
00:11:13,072 --> 00:11:16,609
You're not the only one
going through hard times.

221
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:18,678
You see,

222
00:11:18,744 --> 00:11:21,414
I was forced into the branch hospital.

223
00:11:22,048 --> 00:11:24,316
I've become quite ashamed.

224
00:11:24,383 --> 00:11:26,118
- And that remote work,
- Yes?

225
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:27,953
I was forced to do that.

226
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,822
Talk about stressful!

227
00:11:29,889 --> 00:11:31,290
That Hachisuka,

228
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,559
he's the Internal Medicine Director now.

229
00:11:33,626 --> 00:11:36,796
But that brat
is really lording it over us!

230
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:39,198
- He has gotten that bossy?
- That's right!

231
00:11:39,265 --> 00:11:40,266
Branch Director Hiruma…

232
00:11:40,332 --> 00:11:42,334
I mean, Uncle Hiruma and we

233
00:11:42,401 --> 00:11:44,937
are treated as a nuisance like COVID.

234
00:11:46,172 --> 00:11:49,141
Could this be revenge for back then?

235
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:50,142
What?

236
00:11:52,111 --> 00:11:53,913
<i>When you were Director of Surgery,</i>

237
00:11:53,979 --> 00:11:58,684
<i>Mr. Hachisuka came along</i>
<i>one time as your gopher.</i>

238
00:11:58,751 --> 00:12:00,319
Takashi Ebina,

239
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:03,089
so you're in the next
professor election, huh?

240
00:12:03,155 --> 00:12:05,491
Yes. I would appreciate your support.

241
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:08,260
But I heard you're an unreliable surgeon.

242
00:12:08,327 --> 00:12:09,495
No.

243
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:10,830
Is that right?

244
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:14,667
Well, then maybe
I'll go with this Takashi Torii.

245
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:17,436
- What?
- Torii is a terrible surgeon.

246
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:20,172
What I like are his papers.

247
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:22,241
He's highly regarded overseas.

248
00:12:22,308 --> 00:12:24,276
Those who write papers try to take

249
00:12:24,343 --> 00:12:26,312
all the glory for surgeries
for themselves.

250
00:12:26,378 --> 00:12:27,213
Now, now.

251
00:12:27,279 --> 00:12:28,614
What this guy really wants

252
00:12:28,681 --> 00:12:30,649
is to be the next hospital director.

253
00:12:31,183 --> 00:12:32,017
Really?

254
00:12:32,084 --> 00:12:33,252
Shigeka-chan will be the next

255
00:12:33,319 --> 00:12:34,920
Totei University Hospital Director?

256
00:12:35,988 --> 00:12:37,056
How reassuring!

257
00:12:37,123 --> 00:12:38,157
Give me your support.

258
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:39,358
Of course.

259
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:41,060
- Director Hiruma.
- What?

260
00:12:41,127 --> 00:12:42,762
You have surgery in the morning.

261
00:12:42,828 --> 00:12:44,597
Isn't it about time to leave?

262
00:12:44,663 --> 00:12:46,432
What a stupid thing to say.

263
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:48,734
I'm in the middle
of an important conversation.

264
00:12:49,635 --> 00:12:52,104
In the next election
for hospital director,

265
00:12:52,171 --> 00:12:55,174
please give me your honest vote.

266
00:12:55,241 --> 00:12:56,709
Honest vote?

267
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:58,744
You'll offer bribes like crazy, right?

268
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:02,915
Mama, would you please give these men
a bottle of champagne each?

269
00:13:02,982 --> 00:13:04,450
Certainly. Thank you.

270
00:13:04,517 --> 00:13:05,785
This is wrong!

271
00:13:06,485 --> 00:13:09,221
- We should be leaving.
- Dr. Hachisuka, this is important talk!

272
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:10,589
Why are you interrupting?

273
00:13:10,656 --> 00:13:12,525
You call this important?

274
00:13:12,591 --> 00:13:17,797
There has been an outbreak
of a norovirus variant in this area.

275
00:13:18,397 --> 00:13:19,665
If we caught it before surgery,

276
00:13:19,732 --> 00:13:21,400
there would be big trouble!

277
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:22,601
Dr. Hachisuka!

278
00:13:24,036 --> 00:13:25,437
Shut up, would you?

279
00:13:25,504 --> 00:13:26,939
You infection maniac.

280
00:13:27,606 --> 00:13:29,642
- "Infection maniac?"
- I like it!

281
00:13:29,708 --> 00:13:31,210
I'm sorry about him.

282
00:13:31,277 --> 00:13:33,245
Get out of here, you infection maniac.

283
00:13:37,116 --> 00:13:39,385
<i>The look in Mr. Hachisuka's eyes then…</i>

284
00:13:39,885 --> 00:13:41,253
I'll never forget it.

285
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,455
Did I say that?

286
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:46,292
Even if you don't remember saying it,

287
00:13:46,358 --> 00:13:49,461
it sticks with the person
you said it to, Uncle Hiruma.

288
00:13:49,528 --> 00:13:52,865
Not long after that, Uncle Hiruma,
he quit the Surgery Department.

289
00:13:54,466 --> 00:13:55,768
Cut it out with the "uncle."

290
00:13:56,769 --> 00:13:57,803
Mama,

291
00:13:57,870 --> 00:14:01,040
to brighten things up,
can we get some sushi here?

292
00:14:01,106 --> 00:14:02,308
Sushi?

293
00:14:03,042 --> 00:14:04,143
Hold on a second.

294
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,745
Due to the way things are,

295
00:14:07,379 --> 00:14:10,082
they won't pay a cent
for entertainment expenses.

296
00:14:12,284 --> 00:14:15,020
Hey, you know
those <i>inarizushi</i> sets they have

297
00:14:15,554 --> 00:14:17,223
at the convenience store?

298
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:21,093
Can you get just two of those?

299
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:24,096
I'm just glad you came.
<i>Inarizushi,</i> coming right up.

300
00:14:24,163 --> 00:14:25,264
Thanks!

301
00:14:26,332 --> 00:14:28,067
And put it on my tab.

302
00:14:34,173 --> 00:14:36,175
- Mayako Mama!
- Mama, are you okay?

303
00:14:36,942 --> 00:14:39,578
- Mayako Mama?
- I'm just a little dizzy.

304
00:14:39,645 --> 00:14:40,546
Dizzy?

305
00:14:40,613 --> 00:14:42,214
Dr. Ebina! Run tests!

306
00:14:42,281 --> 00:14:44,717
Yes, sir! We'll run thorough tests
at our hospital!

307
00:14:44,783 --> 00:14:46,085
- Right!
- Are you okay?

308
00:14:46,151 --> 00:14:47,653
Can you get up, Mama?

309
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:48,687
Slowly.

310
00:14:53,492 --> 00:14:57,296
I want to do surgeries!

311
00:14:57,363 --> 00:14:59,598
Well, if it isn't Dr. Daimon.

312
00:15:00,966 --> 00:15:02,935
How long have you been at this hospital?

313
00:15:03,669 --> 00:15:04,670
Who are you?

314
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:08,707
Oh, come on.
How could you possibly forget me?

315
00:15:08,774 --> 00:15:11,677
You know, meeting you
at a place like this,

316
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,145
it feels like fate.

317
00:15:13,212 --> 00:15:14,313
What?

318
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:16,048
To celebrate meeting again,

319
00:15:16,115 --> 00:15:18,317
do you want to join me for a meal of meat?

320
00:15:20,452 --> 00:15:21,287
Meat?

321
00:15:22,655 --> 00:15:24,056
I'll do that!

322
00:15:25,491 --> 00:15:27,393
Okay, see you.

323
00:15:27,459 --> 00:15:28,394
See you.

324
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,801
Who was that guy?

325
00:15:38,137 --> 00:15:41,206
I want to do surgeries!

326
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:44,777
I want to do surgeries!

327
00:15:44,843 --> 00:15:45,744
VIP ROOM A

328
00:15:45,811 --> 00:15:46,645
Shigeka-chan.

329
00:15:47,546 --> 00:15:49,415
This is a wonderful room you got for me.

330
00:15:50,382 --> 00:15:51,417
<i>Thank you.</i>

331
00:15:51,917 --> 00:15:52,918
Maya-chan,

332
00:15:52,985 --> 00:15:55,554
I'm glad you like it.

333
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:56,789
That room there,

334
00:15:56,855 --> 00:15:59,858
<i>it's this hospital's VIP room.</i>

335
00:15:59,925 --> 00:16:03,062
We'll run some tests on you
while you're there.

336
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:05,064
If we find anything wrong,

337
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:08,634
we'll operate on you and fix you up, okay?

338
00:16:08,701 --> 00:16:11,203
- Hey!
- You just said "operate," right?

339
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:12,972
- Yes, I did.
- Let me do it!

340
00:16:13,038 --> 00:16:14,673
Don't be ridiculous, you idiot.

341
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:18,110
Damn it! I haven't operated
even once since recovering!

342
00:16:18,177 --> 00:16:19,611
- What do I care?
- Dr. Daimon!

343
00:16:19,678 --> 00:16:20,779
Dr. Daimon!

344
00:16:20,846 --> 00:16:21,981
Dr. Daimon, listen.

345
00:16:22,848 --> 00:16:27,119
Nearly all surgeries have been cut
due to COVID and that Dr. Hachisuka!

346
00:16:27,186 --> 00:16:29,822
Besides, you have just recovered
from an illness. Understand?

347
00:16:29,888 --> 00:16:31,256
- Don't be spoiled!
- You're spitting!

348
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:32,558
Sorry. I'm sorry.

349
00:16:32,624 --> 00:16:35,060
- I'll set her straight later.
- Okay.

350
00:16:35,127 --> 00:16:38,464
Maya-chan, sorry about that.
We had a little interruption.

351
00:16:38,530 --> 00:16:40,165
- Please, continue talking.
- Go ahead.

352
00:16:40,232 --> 00:16:43,369
<i>Shigeka-chan, you seem awfully busy.</i>

353
00:16:43,435 --> 00:16:46,739
If you need anything,
contact me right away. Okay?

354
00:16:46,805 --> 00:16:49,742
I'll zip right over there.
You won't wait long.

355
00:16:50,642 --> 00:16:52,077
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

356
00:16:52,144 --> 00:16:53,278
Your wife is here.

357
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:55,781
- Honey! Oh, my.
- Mrs. Hiruma.

358
00:17:02,554 --> 00:17:04,123
Why are you here today?

359
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:06,291
For my physical exam.

360
00:17:06,358 --> 00:17:08,627
We canceled it last year because of COVID,

361
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:11,196
so you said I should get
thoroughly tested this year.

362
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:14,466
It was you who made reservations
for three days and two nights.

363
00:17:15,134 --> 00:17:16,402
Oh, that's right.

364
00:17:16,468 --> 00:17:17,469
It's today?

365
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:21,607
I wish I wasn't
at this miserable branch hospital.

366
00:17:21,673 --> 00:17:25,244
I much prefer my usual VIP room
at the main hospital.

367
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:26,245
I'm sorry.

368
00:17:26,311 --> 00:17:28,147
Right now,
the main hospital has been taken over

369
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:29,882
by Dr. Hachisuka of Internal Medicine.

370
00:17:29,948 --> 00:17:31,250
Oh, dear.

371
00:17:31,984 --> 00:17:32,985
You mean,

372
00:17:33,519 --> 00:17:35,354
you can't free up the VIP room for me?

373
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:38,490
He's someone who has absolutely
no ideas of what's best

374
00:17:38,557 --> 00:17:40,059
for his superiors.

375
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:41,960
That's right.

376
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:48,067
Even I can't do a single thing about it.

377
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:02,514
Covering up for that Ginza club mama…

378
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:04,116
I won't do it.

379
00:18:06,985 --> 00:18:08,821
"Ginza club mama?"

380
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:12,691
What's that about?

381
00:18:13,559 --> 00:18:15,661
Well, you see…

382
00:18:16,395 --> 00:18:19,498
It would take a really long time
to explain.

383
00:18:19,565 --> 00:18:22,768
- Go ahead.
- You know that Maestro Club?

384
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:29,708
There's a 92-year-old guy
from that named Ginza Coverup.

385
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:31,009
He's here now.

386
00:18:31,076 --> 00:18:33,345
Really?

387
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:41,186
Excuse me.

388
00:18:42,321 --> 00:18:44,289
- Hello.
- Hello.

389
00:18:44,356 --> 00:18:46,592
Excuse me. Where is Dr. Hiruma?

390
00:18:47,326 --> 00:18:50,195
We were video conferencing,
but it got cut off.

391
00:18:50,262 --> 00:18:53,065
He's dealing with something now,
so I came in his stead.

392
00:18:54,366 --> 00:18:56,568
When did your dizzy spells begin?

393
00:18:58,770 --> 00:19:00,873
Off and on since about a year ago.

394
00:19:01,907 --> 00:19:03,842
I think it's just psychological.

395
00:19:03,909 --> 00:19:06,345
I've been mentally exhausted from COVID.

396
00:19:07,079 --> 00:19:10,015
Then let's do blood tests
and a CT just to be safe.

397
00:19:10,849 --> 00:19:12,017
I'll take you there.

398
00:19:12,084 --> 00:19:13,619
- You can walk, right?
- Yes.

399
00:19:16,955 --> 00:19:17,956
Mayako Niki,

400
00:19:18,023 --> 00:19:19,258
it has been a while.

401
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:21,827
Oh, my! Dr. Hachisuka!

402
00:19:21,894 --> 00:19:23,462
You remember me?

403
00:19:23,529 --> 00:19:25,297
Of course, I do.

404
00:19:25,364 --> 00:19:27,799
I often see you on TV.

405
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:31,570
I know how busy you are,
but you still came to see me?

406
00:19:31,637 --> 00:19:33,138
You are a VIP after all.

407
00:19:33,205 --> 00:19:34,039
Of course.

408
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:37,309
I've put this man in charge,
so ask him anything.

409
00:19:37,376 --> 00:19:38,277
What?

410
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:40,679
It's nice to meet you. I'm Dr. Korogi.

411
00:19:40,746 --> 00:19:42,848
Oh, my. Such a handsome doctor.

412
00:19:44,116 --> 00:19:45,984
Come with me. We'll get some tests done.

413
00:19:50,556 --> 00:19:51,690
Thank you.

414
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:56,161
You know,

415
00:19:56,662 --> 00:20:00,699
you should smile a little more
like this doctor.

416
00:20:00,766 --> 00:20:03,302
Medicine is a service industry, right?

417
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:04,703
I won't.

418
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:07,072
I am terribly sorry.

419
00:20:07,139 --> 00:20:09,174
She has not been properly trained.

420
00:20:09,841 --> 00:20:10,842
Dr. Daimon,

421
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:12,878
goodbye.

422
00:20:18,350 --> 00:20:19,818
What's with that guy?

423
00:20:21,019 --> 00:20:22,221
Who is he?

424
00:20:33,298 --> 00:20:36,668
We will now begin the combined
main hospital

425
00:20:36,735 --> 00:20:39,905
and branch hospital conference.

426
00:20:45,978 --> 00:20:49,982
The first case is Hideo Anzai,
male, age 55.

427
00:20:50,048 --> 00:20:52,818
His diagnosis is progressive
type 4 stomach cancer.

428
00:20:52,884 --> 00:20:56,355
Anaplastic adenocarcinoma was detected
in a stomach ulceration.

429
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:57,556
Let me operate!

430
00:20:58,857 --> 00:21:01,793
The surgery will be
a pylorus preserving gastrectomy.

431
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:05,397
I will operate via laparoscopy.

432
00:21:05,464 --> 00:21:07,266
I'm counting on you, Dr. Kaji.

433
00:21:07,332 --> 00:21:08,900
Yes, sir.

434
00:21:10,369 --> 00:21:12,037
Internal Medicine Director…

435
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:13,505
I mean, Acting Hospital Director.

436
00:21:15,307 --> 00:21:16,408
Is this acceptable?

437
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:18,110
I won't do it.

438
00:21:18,176 --> 00:21:19,878
- Hey? What's with that?
- Are you kidding?

439
00:21:21,179 --> 00:21:22,481
Silence!

440
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:25,417
You're spreading droplets.

441
00:21:26,985 --> 00:21:28,353
I won't allow surgery.

442
00:21:29,321 --> 00:21:31,390
We'll treat it with a FOLFOX regimen.

443
00:21:35,694 --> 00:21:37,195
The next patient, please.

444
00:21:38,263 --> 00:21:42,200
The second case is Fumiko Kuramoto,
female, age 70.

445
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:44,736
Her diagnosis is ascending colon cancer.

446
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:46,371
Let me operate!

447
00:21:46,438 --> 00:21:48,106
She should get surgery right away.

448
00:21:48,173 --> 00:21:49,141
I won't do it.

449
00:21:49,207 --> 00:21:50,509
Hey!

450
00:21:51,777 --> 00:21:54,980
You keep on saying, "I won't do it."

451
00:21:55,047 --> 00:21:57,215
That expression

452
00:21:57,282 --> 00:22:00,285
is Michiko Daimon's patented phrase.

453
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:02,654
Isn't that right, Dr. Daimon?

454
00:22:02,721 --> 00:22:04,156
Look this way. Okay?

455
00:22:04,222 --> 00:22:07,225
Therefore,
she will be treated with medication.

456
00:22:07,292 --> 00:22:09,061
- I was talking.
- Next.

457
00:22:11,263 --> 00:22:14,299
Case three is Kazuya Koto, male, age 33.

458
00:22:14,366 --> 00:22:16,335
His diagnosis
is multiple liver metastases.

459
00:22:16,401 --> 00:22:17,536
I'll do it!

460
00:22:17,602 --> 00:22:19,071
I won't do it.

461
00:22:19,638 --> 00:22:20,806
I will do it.

462
00:22:21,873 --> 00:22:24,376
Keep that up and these patients will die!

463
00:22:24,443 --> 00:22:25,977
Dr. Daimon,

464
00:22:26,044 --> 00:22:27,412
I think you should be

465
00:22:27,479 --> 00:22:30,749
fully aware of the danger
of becoming infected.

466
00:22:31,316 --> 00:22:33,585
Since there is a risk of new infections,

467
00:22:33,652 --> 00:22:36,521
we will refrain from surgeries
as much as possible.

468
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:44,062
Test results for the VIP patient are in.

469
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:50,335
Who is this guy?

470
00:22:51,169 --> 00:22:52,037
He's a newbie.

471
00:22:52,104 --> 00:22:52,971
Who the heck are you?

472
00:22:53,638 --> 00:22:56,007
He is a super doctor
that Director Hachisuka

473
00:22:56,074 --> 00:22:57,843
invited to work here.

474
00:22:57,909 --> 00:22:59,044
"Super?"

475
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:01,980
Nice to meet you, surgeons.

476
00:23:02,481 --> 00:23:03,815
I am Dr. Korogi.

477
00:23:04,349 --> 00:23:06,251
His specialty is neurosurgery.

478
00:23:06,318 --> 00:23:07,419
What? Neurosurgery?

479
00:23:07,486 --> 00:23:12,124
He is a world authority
and is called "White Jack" overseas.

480
00:23:12,190 --> 00:23:13,658
A world authority?

481
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:14,793
White Jack?

482
00:23:15,427 --> 00:23:16,661
Oh, so he's a knockoff.

483
00:23:16,728 --> 00:23:19,331
Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka,

484
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:22,434
you keep ranting about
how you won't allow surgery.

485
00:23:23,335 --> 00:23:25,771
But then you hire
the surgeon Michiko Daimon

486
00:23:25,837 --> 00:23:29,274
and this neurosurgeon, Mr. Korogi.

487
00:23:29,341 --> 00:23:32,644
What's the point of all that?

488
00:23:32,711 --> 00:23:34,646
- Agreed!
- Agreed!

489
00:23:34,713 --> 00:23:36,782
Dr. Korogi

490
00:23:36,848 --> 00:23:40,285
is a talented surgeon
who honed his skill in the US.

491
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:44,589
With the addition of his skills
to our advanced medical care,

492
00:23:45,290 --> 00:23:50,028
it will be possible to achieve
100% perfect treatment.

493
00:23:50,796 --> 00:23:53,465
Report on the VIP patient's test results.

494
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:01,540
- Mayako Mama?
- What?

495
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:02,974
Hold on here.

496
00:24:03,041 --> 00:24:05,377
She is Branch Director Hiruma's patient.

497
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:06,445
Hey,

498
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:10,449
this patient is mine, you know.

499
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:13,118
I will decide on her treatment.

500
00:24:14,553 --> 00:24:15,720
What is her diagnosis?

501
00:24:16,488 --> 00:24:19,124
A mild cerebral infarction

502
00:24:19,191 --> 00:24:20,959
due to a partial
thrombosed cerebral aneurysm.

503
00:24:21,026 --> 00:24:22,894
Cerebral aneurysm?

504
00:24:24,529 --> 00:24:27,933
For that, a vascular coil embolization
should be performed.

505
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:29,768
I agree.

506
00:24:29,835 --> 00:24:32,871
I told you! She is my patient!

507
00:24:33,605 --> 00:24:35,740
We don't need Internal Medicine's opinion!

508
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:36,942
- Agreed!
- Agreed!

509
00:24:37,008 --> 00:24:38,977
We don't need Surgery's interference!

510
00:24:41,947 --> 00:24:42,914
What?

511
00:24:45,417 --> 00:24:46,918
I will do it!

512
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:50,322
I will perform surgery.

513
00:24:52,357 --> 00:24:54,159
How dare you!

514
00:24:54,226 --> 00:24:57,262
I told you Internal Medicine
will administer treatment!

515
00:24:57,329 --> 00:25:00,165
I'm not talking about that.
I'm talking about this.

516
00:25:00,232 --> 00:25:04,169
It's highly unlikely that tiny
of an aneurysm would cause an infarction.

517
00:25:04,236 --> 00:25:07,239
Most likely,
the infarction was caused by--

518
00:25:07,305 --> 00:25:08,406
Director Hachisuka!

519
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:11,443
I detect extreme constriction
in the carotid artery.

520
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:12,844
I see. True.

521
00:25:12,911 --> 00:25:14,946
Then a stent implant should be performed

522
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:16,448
for the carotid artery stenosis.

523
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:17,349
Naturally,

524
00:25:17,415 --> 00:25:19,217
Internal Medicine will handle it.

525
00:25:21,019 --> 00:25:22,487
Objection!

526
00:25:25,290 --> 00:25:27,559
There is unstable plaque
in the carotid artery.

527
00:25:28,126 --> 00:25:29,995
If a stent is implanted,

528
00:25:30,061 --> 00:25:33,598
it could release a clot
and worsen the cerebral infarction.

529
00:25:34,132 --> 00:25:37,536
The best option is a thrombo-intimectomy.

530
00:25:37,602 --> 00:25:38,970
Well done, Dr. Daimon!

531
00:25:39,037 --> 00:25:40,405
Nice work!

532
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:50,248
This is why we can't trust you people!

533
00:25:50,315 --> 00:25:51,216
- Agreed!
- Agreed!

534
00:25:52,951 --> 00:25:57,255
You're so worried about
the spread of infections,

535
00:25:57,322 --> 00:26:01,726
you missed
a crucial carotid artery stenosis.

536
00:26:01,793 --> 00:26:04,930
You have your priorities backwards.

537
00:26:04,996 --> 00:26:08,633
You infection worry-wart maniac.

538
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,838
Silence!

539
00:26:18,476 --> 00:26:19,811
The surgeon will be…

540
00:26:21,012 --> 00:26:22,013
Dr. Korogi.

541
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,181
If you would.

542
00:26:26,351 --> 00:26:28,286
Do you plan on controlling everything?

543
00:26:28,353 --> 00:26:31,923
You're the one who missed
the carotid artery stenosis!

544
00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:34,392
That's right! Surgery should be done
by the Surgery Department!

545
00:26:34,459 --> 00:26:35,760
- Agreed!
- Agreed!

546
00:26:36,528 --> 00:26:38,096
Internal Medicine Director Hachisuka

547
00:26:38,163 --> 00:26:41,266
was given complete control
by the hospital director!

548
00:26:44,369 --> 00:26:46,571
Cut out that creepy "yes, sir!"

549
00:26:47,872 --> 00:26:49,240
You're releasing droplets!

550
00:26:50,375 --> 00:26:52,143
I said cut it out!

551
00:26:53,345 --> 00:26:54,746
Cut it out!

552
00:26:55,413 --> 00:26:57,015
You're releasing droplets!

553
00:27:01,152 --> 00:27:02,153
I see.

554
00:27:02,687 --> 00:27:06,024
So I have two diseases.

555
00:27:06,091 --> 00:27:08,460
It will be just fine. Okay?

556
00:27:08,526 --> 00:27:10,795
You'll be cured for sure. Don't worry.

557
00:27:12,564 --> 00:27:14,232
I guess my luck's run out.

558
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:18,503
I told you, you'll be just fine.

559
00:27:18,570 --> 00:27:20,572
Maya-chan, you see,

560
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:23,174
you've got me, Shigekatsu Hiruma,
with you.

561
00:27:23,241 --> 00:27:25,276
Let's fight this together.

562
00:27:25,343 --> 00:27:26,344
All right?

563
00:27:29,014 --> 00:27:30,682
Will I really be saved?

564
00:27:30,749 --> 00:27:33,418
Of course.

565
00:27:37,555 --> 00:27:40,492
- Excuse me.
- What? What are you doing here?

566
00:27:41,893 --> 00:27:42,894
Don't worry.

567
00:27:42,961 --> 00:27:45,764
Tomorrow, this super doctor,

568
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:48,133
Dr. Korogi, will operate on you.

569
00:27:48,199 --> 00:27:49,334
Hold on!

570
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:51,169
Before the surgery,

571
00:27:51,236 --> 00:27:52,937
let's get more thorough tests.

572
00:27:53,738 --> 00:27:55,840
- That's right.
- Dr. Daimon,

573
00:27:55,907 --> 00:27:57,909
you just want to perform the surgery.

574
00:28:00,278 --> 00:28:03,348
- Anyway, more tests need--
- Enough of that!

575
00:28:03,415 --> 00:28:07,152
Do you plan to use the patient
as practice for your rehabilitation?

576
00:28:07,719 --> 00:28:09,654
- What?
- Rehabilitation?

577
00:28:10,755 --> 00:28:14,392
She just recovered from Lassa fever.

578
00:28:15,326 --> 00:28:17,195
Lassa fever?

579
00:28:17,262 --> 00:28:18,196
What's that?

580
00:28:20,365 --> 00:28:21,866
You certainly don't want

581
00:28:22,434 --> 00:28:25,770
your life in the hands of a doctor
who has just recovered from an illness.

582
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:27,605
No.

583
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:29,741
Dr. Korogi.

584
00:28:33,311 --> 00:28:35,680
As planned, I will operate.

585
00:28:35,747 --> 00:28:36,715
Wait!

586
00:28:36,781 --> 00:28:39,951
In the name of the Totei University
Hospital Surgery Department,

587
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:41,753
we will save her!

588
00:28:41,820 --> 00:28:44,089
That sounds very bold,

589
00:28:44,155 --> 00:28:48,226
but your wife is looking for you
in the branch hospital.

590
00:28:48,293 --> 00:28:49,360
You're kidding.

591
00:28:49,427 --> 00:28:51,596
Your wife is hospitalized?

592
00:28:51,663 --> 00:28:54,065
No. Just for tests.
She's perfectly healthy.

593
00:28:54,132 --> 00:28:55,533
Your wife is waiting.

594
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:57,769
Return to the branch hospital.

595
00:28:57,836 --> 00:28:59,370
You sure are a bossy one.

596
00:28:59,437 --> 00:29:00,772
I feel bad for your wife.

597
00:29:00,839 --> 00:29:02,107
Hurry up and see her.

598
00:29:02,173 --> 00:29:04,175
- I won't!
- You need to go!

599
00:29:04,242 --> 00:29:05,076
No!

600
00:29:05,143 --> 00:29:06,478
- Dr. Hachisuka,
- What?

601
00:29:07,011 --> 00:29:09,714
I'll leave myself in the hands
of this super doctor.

602
00:29:10,882 --> 00:29:12,217
I am in your care.

603
00:29:15,019 --> 00:29:16,221
You can count on us.

604
00:29:17,455 --> 00:29:20,458
Please rest well
to prepare for the surgery.

605
00:29:20,525 --> 00:29:21,426
Thank you.

606
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:24,629
Then, Branch Director Hiruma,

607
00:29:25,163 --> 00:29:26,898
I will be going.

608
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:32,137
You… promotion maniac.

609
00:29:40,845 --> 00:29:41,846
Just now…

610
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:46,117
what did Dr. Hachisuka say
while he was leaving?

611
00:29:47,385 --> 00:29:48,486
You…

612
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:50,889
promotion maniac.

613
00:29:54,759 --> 00:29:58,897
That Dr. Hachisuka really does hold
a grudge about that.

614
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:00,832
You infection maniac.

615
00:30:03,701 --> 00:30:05,837
I'm hyperventilating!

616
00:30:15,947 --> 00:30:20,251
So they still won't let
Ms. Daimon operate?

617
00:30:20,318 --> 00:30:22,921
She hasn't gotten anything.
It's a big problem.

618
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:26,958
How come that new Korogi guy
at Totei University is called "super"?

619
00:30:27,025 --> 00:30:29,060
He's a member of the super elite

620
00:30:29,127 --> 00:30:31,529
who was at Columbia Central Hospital
in New York.

621
00:30:31,596 --> 00:30:34,933
Then didn't you work with him, Ms. Daimon?

622
00:30:34,999 --> 00:30:36,801
I don't remember him at all.

623
00:30:36,868 --> 00:30:39,304
Michiko is terrible at remembering faces.

624
00:30:39,370 --> 00:30:42,540
But she remembers
a patient's organs and veins in no time.

625
00:30:42,607 --> 00:30:46,544
She still doesn't even remember
my face or name.

626
00:30:46,611 --> 00:30:47,912
You can't be serious!

627
00:30:47,979 --> 00:30:49,581
I remember!

628
00:30:49,647 --> 00:30:50,648
Janno.

629
00:30:51,316 --> 00:30:52,250
It's Suzuno.

630
00:30:53,751 --> 00:30:54,586
It is?

631
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:57,889
I win!

632
00:30:57,956 --> 00:30:59,224
<i>Tsumo </i>only!

633
00:30:59,290 --> 00:31:01,059
- Time to go home!
- What a low hand!

634
00:31:01,125 --> 00:31:02,994
Wait! One more hand!

635
00:31:03,061 --> 00:31:04,963
I've got surgery tomorrow. Goodbye!

636
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:07,298
- You sure run away easily.
- Bye!

637
00:31:07,365 --> 00:31:08,933
Win and run!

638
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:12,503
What's wrong?

639
00:31:12,570 --> 00:31:14,706
- I remembered!
- What?

640
00:31:15,273 --> 00:31:16,541
That guy!

641
00:31:17,108 --> 00:31:18,176
That guy?

642
00:31:19,077 --> 00:31:21,813
That super doctor.

643
00:31:34,926 --> 00:31:39,964
We will now perform Mayako Niki's
carotid artery thrombo-intimectomy.

644
00:31:41,499 --> 00:31:44,168
Though I'm reluctant,
I'll be your assistant.

645
00:31:44,235 --> 00:31:47,005
Mr. Kaji, try and keep up. All right?

646
00:31:47,071 --> 00:31:48,273
Don't talk to me like that.

647
00:31:48,339 --> 00:31:50,275
Don't lose your temper in the OR.

648
00:31:54,712 --> 00:31:55,880
I will begin.

649
00:31:57,181 --> 00:31:58,383
I'm counting on you.

650
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:02,987
At last, we can witness
Dr. Korogi's skills at work.

651
00:32:04,555 --> 00:32:08,760
BP 118 over 79, pulse 81, normal sinus.

652
00:32:08,826 --> 00:32:10,061
- Scalpel.
- Here.

653
00:32:16,834 --> 00:32:18,002
- Bovie.
- Here.

654
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:33,351
Exposing the common carotid. Metz.

655
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:34,352
Here.

656
00:32:40,091 --> 00:32:42,160
He's really fast.

657
00:32:43,094 --> 00:32:44,095
Fast doesn't mean good.

658
00:32:44,162 --> 00:32:45,530
Oh, yes.

659
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:52,170
So this is what
faster than your eye can see means.

660
00:32:52,236 --> 00:32:54,172
White Jack is quite amazing!

661
00:32:55,006 --> 00:32:57,842
I can see why you scouted him,
Director Hachisuka.

662
00:33:02,981 --> 00:33:06,884
That Dr. Korogi is really fast,
but will Maya-chan be all right?

663
00:33:06,951 --> 00:33:08,252
I'm worried too.

664
00:33:12,423 --> 00:33:14,058
- Dr. Ebina.
- Yes?

665
00:33:14,125 --> 00:33:15,526
What are you doing here?

666
00:33:16,027 --> 00:33:19,964
I'm worried about you
because you're worried about Mayako Mama.

667
00:33:21,899 --> 00:33:23,301
You're way too close.

668
00:33:24,202 --> 00:33:25,269
Yes, sir.

669
00:33:26,537 --> 00:33:30,274
I hate to give them credit,

670
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:33,311
but I sure do hope
this surgery is a success.

671
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:35,513
You better believe it.

672
00:33:35,580 --> 00:33:38,383
If it looks like he'll mess up…

673
00:33:39,250 --> 00:33:40,752
I'll rush over there,

674
00:33:42,053 --> 00:33:44,422
grab a scalpel and operate.

675
00:33:44,489 --> 00:33:47,658
Branch Director Hiruma,
for over a decade now…

676
00:33:48,159 --> 00:33:50,395
you've been trying so hard
to become director,

677
00:33:50,461 --> 00:33:52,330
you haven't operated even once.

678
00:33:52,897 --> 00:33:56,000
It has been that long since I operated?

679
00:33:56,067 --> 00:33:57,735
Yes. At worst…

680
00:33:58,669 --> 00:33:59,604
you could kill her.

681
00:34:01,973 --> 00:34:03,107
You're right.

682
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:05,209
Carotid artery branching exposed.

683
00:34:05,276 --> 00:34:07,178
Exposing internal carotid artery.
Mosquito.

684
00:34:07,245 --> 00:34:08,146
Here.

685
00:34:15,119 --> 00:34:16,120
Hey.

686
00:34:16,187 --> 00:34:17,989
Don't you think you're going too fast?

687
00:34:18,489 --> 00:34:20,792
Be more careful around the carotid artery.

688
00:34:20,858 --> 00:34:24,796
In the US, lead surgeons perform
10 to 20 surgeries a day.

689
00:34:24,862 --> 00:34:26,464
They require speed.

690
00:34:26,531 --> 00:34:28,032
Enough bragging.

691
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:31,202
Be more careful there.

692
00:34:31,269 --> 00:34:34,405
At this rate,
we'll easily be done by lunchtime.

693
00:34:35,173 --> 00:34:37,075
I'm in the mood for Italian.

694
00:34:37,642 --> 00:34:38,476
Join me?

695
00:34:38,543 --> 00:34:39,510
What?

696
00:34:39,577 --> 00:34:41,212
Hitting on women in the OR.

697
00:34:41,279 --> 00:34:42,513
Even I wouldn't do that.

698
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,582
- That's for sure.
- What?

699
00:34:45,149 --> 00:34:46,284
Sorry.

700
00:34:54,792 --> 00:34:55,793
Dr. Korogi,

701
00:34:55,860 --> 00:34:57,395
is it going well?

702
00:34:58,196 --> 00:34:59,864
Yes. It's going perfectly.

703
00:35:01,132 --> 00:35:03,267
Opening the carotid artery.
Lower my loupes.

704
00:35:03,334 --> 00:35:05,002
Yes, sir. Excuse me.

705
00:35:06,370 --> 00:35:07,772
- Scalpel.
- Here.

706
00:35:17,115 --> 00:35:19,884
BP has dropped drastically to the 60s!

707
00:35:19,951 --> 00:35:21,018
How come?

708
00:35:23,221 --> 00:35:24,489
A blood clot?

709
00:35:24,555 --> 00:35:25,857
Brain waves are normal.

710
00:35:27,525 --> 00:35:28,860
Then what is it?

711
00:35:33,397 --> 00:35:35,099
Oh, I'm going!

712
00:35:35,166 --> 00:35:37,168
No! You can't! Calm down!

713
00:35:37,235 --> 00:35:38,870
If you go, you'll kill her!

714
00:35:42,340 --> 00:35:44,242
You said it was going well!

715
00:35:44,742 --> 00:35:46,010
What is the cause?

716
00:35:47,778 --> 00:35:49,914
- I don't know.
- What?

717
00:35:50,414 --> 00:35:52,250
What will you do, White Jack?

718
00:35:52,316 --> 00:35:53,951
What will you do?

719
00:35:54,018 --> 00:35:56,821
BP in the 50s. Saturation 90%!

720
00:36:18,809 --> 00:36:19,877
Oh, dear…

721
00:36:34,258 --> 00:36:35,726
Demon?

722
00:36:38,429 --> 00:36:39,397
Out of the way!

723
00:36:41,098 --> 00:36:42,200
Get the ultrasound.

724
00:36:42,266 --> 00:36:44,335
- I'll cut the chest cloth. Here.
- Yes.

725
00:36:54,512 --> 00:36:56,414
The heart. I knew it.

726
00:36:57,081 --> 00:36:58,516
Acute heart failure.

727
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:02,753
You missed a myxoma in the right atrium.

728
00:37:08,192 --> 00:37:09,360
He missed it?

729
00:37:09,427 --> 00:37:11,195
One more procedure!

730
00:37:11,262 --> 00:37:12,797
Right atrium myxoma removal.

731
00:37:12,863 --> 00:37:14,632
You'll open her heart like this?

732
00:37:14,699 --> 00:37:16,534
- Prep the heart-lung machine.
- Right.

733
00:37:18,135 --> 00:37:20,137
You continue the thrombo-intimectomy.

734
00:37:20,204 --> 00:37:22,740
The neck and heart simultaneously?
That's insane!

735
00:37:23,774 --> 00:37:25,743
Dr. Daimon, don't do it!

736
00:37:25,810 --> 00:37:28,145
Dr. Korogi says it's insane.

737
00:37:28,212 --> 00:37:30,381
And you just recovered.
How can you operate?

738
00:37:30,448 --> 00:37:31,716
Get out of the OR!

739
00:37:31,782 --> 00:37:34,852
Stop your babbling.
The carotid is blocked, so hurry!

740
00:37:34,919 --> 00:37:36,153
- Scalpel.
- Here.

741
00:37:38,522 --> 00:37:39,824
I am the head surgeon.

742
00:37:40,491 --> 00:37:42,994
You're the one who missed
the right atrium myxoma.

743
00:37:43,060 --> 00:37:44,528
Shut up until you fix your mistake.

744
00:37:45,796 --> 00:37:47,732
It's too risky to cut open one more place!

745
00:37:48,499 --> 00:37:51,936
Only 100% successful operations
should be performed.

746
00:37:52,503 --> 00:37:53,804
I'll end this surgery.

747
00:37:53,871 --> 00:37:56,073
Enough of your arrogant "yes, sirs!"

748
00:37:56,140 --> 00:37:58,609
What will happen to her
if you close her up now?

749
00:37:58,676 --> 00:38:01,379
It's better than performing risky surgery.

750
00:38:01,445 --> 00:38:03,381
So you're running away again.

751
00:38:04,682 --> 00:38:05,983
What are you talking about?

752
00:38:10,187 --> 00:38:12,490
This surgery has gone off the rails!

753
00:38:12,556 --> 00:38:13,858
The carotid is hard enough,

754
00:38:13,924 --> 00:38:17,061
but simultaneously removing a myxoma
is far too risky!

755
00:38:17,128 --> 00:38:19,330
It will kill the patient!

756
00:38:19,897 --> 00:38:21,532
I can't be part of this surgery.

757
00:38:21,599 --> 00:38:22,833
I'm leaving!

758
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:25,436
Hey!

759
00:38:26,504 --> 00:38:27,505
Okay.

760
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:30,207
Okay, removing thrombosis lining.

761
00:38:30,274 --> 00:38:31,942
- Lining clamp.
- Here.

762
00:38:39,483 --> 00:38:40,785
Dr. Daimon!

763
00:38:40,851 --> 00:38:41,952
Stop!

764
00:38:42,019 --> 00:38:44,422
For a surgeon, she sure is stupid.

765
00:38:45,089 --> 00:38:47,491
You won't get away with this!

766
00:38:48,693 --> 00:38:50,294
If you fail,

767
00:38:50,961 --> 00:38:53,831
it will be 100% your fault!

768
00:38:58,602 --> 00:39:01,672
I will not fail.

769
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:14,652
Well said!

770
00:39:15,252 --> 00:39:18,122
- Michiko Daimon!
- You can do it, Dr. Daimon!

771
00:39:19,123 --> 00:39:20,725
Thank you!

772
00:39:20,791 --> 00:39:22,193
Thank you!

773
00:39:49,153 --> 00:39:51,088
- Opening right atrium. 11 scalpel.
- Here.

774
00:40:00,998 --> 00:40:02,166
- Metz.
- Here.

775
00:40:26,891 --> 00:40:28,259
Myxoma removed.

776
00:40:28,759 --> 00:40:30,761
Closing with atrial septum patch.

777
00:40:30,828 --> 00:40:31,996
5-0 monofilament.

778
00:40:32,062 --> 00:40:32,897
Here.

779
00:40:55,186 --> 00:40:56,086
Vitals?

780
00:40:56,153 --> 00:40:59,924
BP 108 over 69, pulse 72, normal sinus.

781
00:41:00,658 --> 00:41:01,826
We're done.

782
00:41:30,955 --> 00:41:32,223
About now,

783
00:41:32,289 --> 00:41:34,191
Branch Director Hiruma
is crying tears of joy.

784
00:41:34,258 --> 00:41:35,493
Well done, Dr. Daimon.

785
00:41:35,559 --> 00:41:37,728
- Well done.
- Ms. Daimon.

786
00:41:38,295 --> 00:41:39,430
Congrats on your comeback.

787
00:41:40,831 --> 00:41:41,832
Thank you.

788
00:41:51,542 --> 00:41:54,678
Thank goodness, Maya-chan. I'm so glad.

789
00:41:54,745 --> 00:41:57,915
That was a rough surgery. You did well.

790
00:41:57,982 --> 00:41:59,650
Branch Director Hiruma…

791
00:41:59,717 --> 00:42:02,920
- Well…
- I'll see you…

792
00:42:03,721 --> 00:42:07,057
- at Club Maya again.
- I'll be there too.

793
00:42:17,301 --> 00:42:18,302
Maya-chan…

794
00:42:19,770 --> 00:42:21,739
I mean Hana-chan!

795
00:42:24,041 --> 00:42:25,276
"Maya-chan?"

796
00:42:25,342 --> 00:42:26,877
I never said that.

797
00:42:26,944 --> 00:42:28,312
- You're hearing things.
- Yes.

798
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:30,848
Mrs. Hiruma's physical exam
has been completed.

799
00:42:30,915 --> 00:42:33,517
Is that right? That's great.

800
00:42:33,584 --> 00:42:35,352
What were the results?

801
00:42:35,419 --> 00:42:38,022
There's not a single thing wrong with me.

802
00:42:38,088 --> 00:42:39,557
Congratulations.

803
00:42:40,090 --> 00:42:43,894
There's a bag I would like you
to buy to celebrate.

804
00:42:43,961 --> 00:42:46,230
Right now, with COVID,

805
00:42:46,297 --> 00:42:49,199
things are tight for the hospital.

806
00:42:49,266 --> 00:42:50,868
Incidentally, how much is it?

807
00:42:50,935 --> 00:42:54,838
About the cost of ten visits
to a Ginza hostess club.

808
00:42:54,905 --> 00:42:56,307
That is…

809
00:42:57,207 --> 00:42:58,108
too expensive.

810
00:42:58,175 --> 00:43:00,844
I have the goods on you!

811
00:43:07,518 --> 00:43:08,586
I'll buy it.

812
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:17,628
You did quite well.

813
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:22,199
I respect you for actually performing
such reckless surgery.

814
00:43:23,667 --> 00:43:25,436
You ran away again.

815
00:43:26,670 --> 00:43:28,906
Don't say such scandalous things.

816
00:43:28,973 --> 00:43:31,442
Unlike you, Dr. Daimon,

817
00:43:31,508 --> 00:43:33,777
I know how to avoid a crisis.

818
00:43:35,212 --> 00:43:37,214
Today, you happened to succeed.

819
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:41,218
But by from experience, that operation
had a 90% chance of failure,

820
00:43:41,285 --> 00:43:43,354
and should never have been done.

821
00:43:45,289 --> 00:43:46,690
I remembered.

822
00:43:48,192 --> 00:43:52,262
When New York was in lockdown,
you made excuses and ran away.

823
00:45:01,231 --> 00:45:05,202
<i>I'm surprised you made it back alive,</i>
<i>Dr. Daimon.</i>

824
00:45:06,170 --> 00:45:10,741
Several of your doctor friends
went to the ICU and died, right?

825
00:45:10,808 --> 00:45:11,975
Dozens did!

826
00:45:13,343 --> 00:45:15,879
That is very unfortunate.

827
00:45:35,599 --> 00:45:37,701
If I stay here, I'll be killed.

828
00:45:51,548 --> 00:45:52,883
I'll have you know…

829
00:45:53,383 --> 00:45:55,452
I didn't run away.

830
00:45:56,286 --> 00:46:00,290
Anyone who already knows the risk
but doesn't avoid it…

831
00:46:02,192 --> 00:46:03,527
is just stupid.

832
00:46:05,496 --> 00:46:07,664
I'll gladly be stupid.

833
00:46:07,731 --> 00:46:09,666
It's better than being a coward.

834
00:46:10,667 --> 00:46:14,571
Patients want to escape too,
but they can't run away.

835
00:46:14,638 --> 00:46:17,174
They put their life in the hands
of their surgeon!

836
00:46:19,143 --> 00:46:21,512
Don't you run away again, stupid!

837
00:46:31,722 --> 00:46:33,457
I won't forget this!

838
00:46:36,560 --> 00:46:40,164
Michiko Daimon!

839
00:47:12,062 --> 00:47:14,364
MICHIKO DAIMON
PLACE OF BIRTH: KURE CITY, HIROSHIMA

840
00:47:15,599 --> 00:47:17,634
This feels so nice!

841
00:47:18,602 --> 00:47:22,172
Operations are the best!

842
00:47:23,106 --> 00:47:23,941
SURGERY BRANCH

843
00:47:24,007 --> 00:47:26,643
Maya-chan,
congratulations on your release.

844
00:47:26,710 --> 00:47:28,679
Thank you, Shigeka-chan.

845
00:47:31,548 --> 00:47:33,517
Thank you for all you've done.

846
00:47:34,318 --> 00:47:36,153
Now that my life has been saved,

847
00:47:36,220 --> 00:47:37,354
I'll fight COVID

848
00:47:37,421 --> 00:47:39,223
and keep my business open.

849
00:47:39,289 --> 00:47:40,624
You can do it!

850
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:41,825
Everyone,

851
00:47:41,892 --> 00:47:43,560
please pay me a visit.

852
00:47:43,627 --> 00:47:46,063
- Right away!
- I'll go to observe and contribute!

853
00:47:48,131 --> 00:47:51,301
I'll give you special treatment,
Dr. Korogi.

854
00:47:52,102 --> 00:47:54,938
You successfully performed
that difficult operation,

855
00:47:55,005 --> 00:47:56,373
so I really owe you!

856
00:47:58,342 --> 00:47:59,309
You're welcome.

857
00:48:02,045 --> 00:48:03,347
Excuse me.

858
00:48:03,847 --> 00:48:05,682
Well, Mayako Mama.

859
00:48:05,749 --> 00:48:08,385
Congratulations on your release.

860
00:48:09,152 --> 00:48:11,822
- Who is this?
- Excuse me.

861
00:48:13,190 --> 00:48:16,326
I also heard your wife had a physical exam
and was found

862
00:48:16,393 --> 00:48:18,662
to be in perfect health.

863
00:48:18,729 --> 00:48:21,131
Good health, secure home.

864
00:48:21,198 --> 00:48:24,201
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

865
00:48:24,268 --> 00:48:25,836
- This is a melon.
- Okay.

866
00:48:27,905 --> 00:48:29,539
This is the bill.

867
00:48:30,807 --> 00:48:32,409
Hold on here.

868
00:48:33,110 --> 00:48:35,145
The way things are now,

869
00:48:35,212 --> 00:48:38,548
the hospital is in dire financial straits.

870
00:48:39,249 --> 00:48:40,584
SURGICAL FEES FOR DR. DAIMON

871
00:48:40,651 --> 00:48:43,320
There's no way we can pay this.
This is insane.

872
00:48:43,387 --> 00:48:46,356
- Excuse me. You have a visitor.
- What?

873
00:48:46,423 --> 00:48:47,524
Shimo-chan!

874
00:48:49,660 --> 00:48:51,528
Thank you so much for coming.

875
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:53,697
"Thank you for coming?"

876
00:48:53,764 --> 00:48:55,198
I'm so happy for you.

877
00:48:55,265 --> 00:48:56,667
Thank you.

878
00:48:57,234 --> 00:48:58,402
Excuse me.

879
00:48:59,102 --> 00:49:00,637
May I ask who you are?

880
00:49:02,239 --> 00:49:06,109
He is a customer
who provides me with immense support.

881
00:49:06,176 --> 00:49:07,344
A real fat cat.

882
00:49:08,412 --> 00:49:10,547
Branch Director Hiruma is in a pinch.

883
00:49:10,614 --> 00:49:13,083
Just by bouquet size alone,
he's totally outdone.

884
00:49:13,150 --> 00:49:16,119
I heard Mayako owes you a whole lot.

885
00:49:18,255 --> 00:49:21,491
Please take this
as a token of my appreciation.

886
00:49:21,558 --> 00:49:22,392
Oh, my.

887
00:49:22,459 --> 00:49:26,196
Actually, this kind of thing,

888
00:49:26,263 --> 00:49:28,365
I'm unable to accept.

889
00:49:28,432 --> 00:49:32,536
Maybe Dr. Korogi, whom I owe
my life to, will accept it.

890
00:49:34,304 --> 00:49:35,439
Here.

891
00:49:41,845 --> 00:49:43,981
My car is waiting downstairs.

892
00:49:44,047 --> 00:49:44,881
See you later.

893
00:49:46,683 --> 00:49:48,618
- See you.
- See you.

894
00:49:50,854 --> 00:49:52,656
- What was that about?
- Hey there.

895
00:49:52,723 --> 00:49:55,158
You don't plan on taking that, do you?

896
00:49:55,225 --> 00:49:58,395
Don't tell me
you're that corrupt, are you?

897
00:50:03,734 --> 00:50:06,903
- Fine. I'll give it back.
- How about we do this?

898
00:50:06,970 --> 00:50:12,009
The super doctor Dr. Korogi
will get all the credit,

899
00:50:12,075 --> 00:50:14,878
while my Daimon gets the money.

900
00:50:14,945 --> 00:50:16,079
Wait!

901
00:50:18,148 --> 00:50:19,249
Want to see it?

902
00:50:19,316 --> 00:50:20,617
What? Oh, wow!

903
00:50:22,719 --> 00:50:26,523
I have received the payment.
Enjoy the melon.

904
00:50:26,590 --> 00:50:28,025
Goodbye.

905
00:50:28,091 --> 00:50:29,259
How dare he!

906
00:50:30,827 --> 00:50:33,330
- How dare he!
- Hurray!

907
00:50:35,665 --> 00:50:37,534
Michiko Daimon…

908
00:50:38,702 --> 00:50:43,340
To be perfectly frank,
that was impressive.

909
00:50:43,940 --> 00:50:44,975
What?

910
00:50:45,609 --> 00:50:49,579
I have never seen
such a beautiful operation.

911
00:50:56,820 --> 00:50:58,488
Liquid sweetener?

912
00:51:00,323 --> 00:51:02,559
My throat gets dry after surgery.

913
00:51:02,626 --> 00:51:03,760
Not your throat.

914
00:51:03,827 --> 00:51:04,828
Your brain.

915
00:51:05,629 --> 00:51:07,964
You used to be a surgeon. You understand.

916
00:51:13,537 --> 00:51:18,408
Now, I want to see more of your surgeries.

917
00:51:21,611 --> 00:51:24,114
Surgeries aren't for watching.
They're for doing.

918
00:51:24,714 --> 00:51:26,149
Let me rephrase that.

919
00:51:30,587 --> 00:51:31,855
From now on,

920
00:51:31,922 --> 00:51:35,892
I would like you to work
as my right-hand woman.

921
00:51:38,628 --> 00:51:40,864
Your… right…

922
00:51:40,931 --> 00:51:42,399
Right-hand what?

923
00:51:43,867 --> 00:51:47,003
I can't understand you.
You're not making any sense at all!

924
00:51:47,070 --> 00:51:48,672
I want you to

925
00:51:49,439 --> 00:51:52,609
perform surgeries to your heart's content.

926
00:51:58,482 --> 00:51:59,449
Are you serious?

927
00:52:01,451 --> 00:52:02,686
I'm serious.

928
00:52:07,491 --> 00:52:10,560
I will!

929
00:52:18,668 --> 00:52:19,769
I won't do that.

930
00:52:29,679 --> 00:52:30,947
<i>She hates groups,</i>

931
00:52:31,014 --> 00:52:32,149
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

932
00:52:32,215 --> 00:52:33,917
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

933
00:52:34,551 --> 00:52:37,821
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

934
00:52:37,888 --> 00:52:39,356
<i>to work her way up.</i>

935
00:52:43,960 --> 00:52:46,129
MICHIKO DAIMON

936
00:52:46,830 --> 00:52:49,065
"Specialty. Surgery."

937
00:52:49,933 --> 00:52:52,702
"Hobby. Surgery."

938
00:53:12,656 --> 00:53:15,525
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

939
00:53:15,592 --> 00:53:18,628
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

940
00:53:19,196 --> 00:53:22,933
All right!

941
00:53:50,193 --> 00:53:51,962
<i>You were far too careless.</i>

942
00:53:52,896 --> 00:53:54,864
No! It was not a business dinner.

943
00:53:54,931 --> 00:53:57,267
This is what gives me stress!

944
00:53:57,334 --> 00:53:59,336
You know, you can be easily replaced.

945
00:53:59,402 --> 00:54:00,537
My fault?

946
00:54:00,604 --> 00:54:02,973
<i>Are you saying</i>
<i>that you don't need me anymore?</i>

947
00:54:03,039 --> 00:54:04,574
Then shut up and watch!

948
00:54:04,641 --> 00:54:05,508
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
